# Java Backend Rules (core module only)

- Use OSGi R7 annotations: @Component, @Reference, @Designate, @ObjectClassDefinition
- Sling Models: @Model(adaptables = ...), injection via @Inject / @ValueMapValue
- Service injection via @Reference (field injection for OSGi components)
- Public methods MUST have Javadoc
- Use SLF4J: private static final Logger LOG = LoggerFactory.getLogger(X.class)
- Validation: reject invalid records (null/blank title, invalid enum, unknown assignee)
  and invalid transitions BEFORE persistence
- Throw meaningful domain exceptions; never swallow exceptions silently
- Use java.time (Instant) for timestamps; serialize as ISO-8601 in JSON
- JSON: use Jackson (com.fasterxml.jackson) consistently — do not mix JSON libraries
- No magic-string paths — declare constants (e.g., in a Paths util)
- Base package for all backend code: com.mysite.core
